\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Pipeline. (A)~A conflict prompt pits a context entity against a parametric entity. (B)~Heads are identified on FP16, locked, and applied unchanged on GPTQ INT4. (C)~Steering is dual-run JuICE: Pass~1 records $h_i$ after $o_{\mathrm  {proj}}$; Pass~2 injects $\alpha h_i$. (D)~The original matcher can score a same-entity wrap as parametric; the question-aware matcher requires the named entity to answer the question; gold-PAR-only counts a leave-context move only if the gold parametric entity is named. Random-$K$ controls (dashed arrow) are a parallel verification reported only for matched cells.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{1}{2}{Pipeline. (A)~A conflict prompt pits a context entity against a parametric entity. (B)~Heads are identified on FP16, locked, and applied unchanged on GPTQ INT4. (C)~Steering is dual-run JuICE: Pass~1 records $h_i$ after $o_{\mathrm {proj}}$; Pass~2 injects $\alpha h_i$. (D)~The original matcher can score a same-entity wrap as parametric; the question-aware matcher requires the named entity to answer the question; gold-PAR-only counts a leave-context move only if the gold parametric entity is named. Random-$K$ controls (dashed arrow) are a parallel verification reported only for matched cells}{figure.1}{}}
